From 614ec4b717cf5488e7d153ada936bbf70ba4f773 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:52:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] TarBase diagnostics: why aggregation underperforms on TarBase

Four independent scripts + shared setup:
- 01 aggregation ladder (raw sum -> equal weight -> log ratio -> background -> rank)
- 02 weighting: concentration of the sum, dropping top-expressed genes
- 03 list quality: per-gene response, TargetScan overlap, evidence type,
     HEK293 origin, list-size curve (all vs same-size random references)
- 04 cell-size confound, residualized scores, fluorescence-vs-mRNA gap

Smoke-tested end to end on synthetic data only; not run on real data.
